        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: শাসানো",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শাসানো — shāsāno — \"to threaten; to warn sternly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ডাকাতরা দোকানদারকে শাসাল, কিন্তু তিনি ভয় পেলেন না। ḍākātrā dokāndārke shāsālô, kintu tini bhôy pelen nā. The robbers threatened the shopkeeper, but he wasn't afraid."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): সেই ডাকাত দোকানদারকে শাসাল, sei ḍākāt dokāndārke shāsālô."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শাসানো (shāsāno) comes down from Sanskrit śāsati, 'instructs, punishes, rules' (CDIAL 12419, which lists Bengali sāsā, 'to punish', and notes the -ānō verb, 'to threaten'). Its root śās- is also the root of শাস্তি, a punishment: to threaten is to hold the punishment over someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
