              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ফাঁসানো (phā̃sāno) comes down from Sanskrit spāśayati, 'causes to be bound' (CDIAL 13814, which lists Bengali phā̃sā, 'to be ensnared'). A ফাঁস is a noose: to frame someone is to slip a noose on them."
